  "id": "DrugBank_DB00997 - MONDO_5224",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Doxorubicin, through its indication for Kaposi's Sarcoma and Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(9;11)(p22;q23), may exert a therapeutic effect on this leukemia subtype. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with Doxorubicin being linked to two distinct leukemia subtypes, both of which are associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation. The overlapping pathways suggest that Doxorubicin may act through shared mechanisms, possibly involving antitumor activity or other biological processes that are relevant to this leukemia type. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Doxorubicin to be repurposed for the treatment of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, though further research is needed to clarify the exact mechanisms and clinical relevance.",
